Inventory of the 172 packages in the Cargo.lock all-target dependency graph, with
399 license texts. Resolved features were refreshed from `cargo metadata` on
2026-11-03, when the crates only the removed demos used (ratatui, crossterm, sha2 and their
dependencies) left the graph; sha2 and its eight dependencies came back that day,
to fingerprint approved project agents, with the texts reproduced from the cached sources.
image and its 22 dependencies joined the graph the same day, for images the read tool sends,
with the texts reproduced from the cached sources and two embedded notices their sources
carry: color_quant's (NeuQuant) and image's JPEG encoder's, from the Independent JPEG Group's
libjpeg. This software is based in part on the work of the Independent JPEG Group.
pulldown-cmark and its dependencies pulldown-cmark-escape and unicase joined the graph
the same day, for the web page /export writes, with the texts reproduced from the cached
sources; memchr's `default` feature is resolved since then.
syntect and two-face joined the graph on 2026-11-04, to highlight code, with bincode, fnv,
once_cell, onig, onig_sys, regex-syntax, same-file, thiserror, thiserror-impl, walkdir and
winapi-util, and cc, find-msvc-tools, pkg-config and shlex to build onig_sys; the texts are
reproduced from the cached sources. onig_sys compiles the Oniguruma C library it bundles into
the binary: its COPYING follows the crate's own license. two-face embeds bat's syntax
definitions: the licenses its acknowledgement listing gives for them follow its own.
sha2's asm features are not enabled; its inactive aarch64 sources say "Implementation
adapted from mbedtls" without naming its revision or license: re-audit before enabling asm.
rustls, tokio-rustls, rustls-native-certs and ring joined the graph on 2026-11-05, for HTTPS,
with rustls-webpki, rustls-pki-types, untrusted, subtle, zeroize, getrandom and
openssl-probe; core-foundation(-sys) and security-framework(-sys) for macOS, and schannel,
windows-sys 0.52.0, windows-targets and its eight windows_* crates for Windows, are locked but
not built on Linux. x11rb, x11rb-protocol and gethostname, in the graph since the X11
clipboard (2026-11-04), got their entries then. Their texts are reproduced from the cached
sources, with ring's once_cell polyfill and fiat-crypto licenses. ring compiles C and assembly
derived from BoringSSL and OpenSSL into the binary, under its LICENSE-BoringSSL and
LICENSE-other-bits.
rmcp joined the graph on 2026-11-05, for MCP servers, with chrono, equivalent, futures and its
seven futures-* crates, indexmap, slab, tokio-stream, tokio-util, tracing, tracing-attributes and
tracing-core, a second sha2 (0.11.1) with block-buffer 0.12.1, const-oid, cpufeatures 0.3.1,
crypto-common 0.2.2, digest 0.11.3 and hybrid-array, and syn 2.0.119 for tracing-attributes;
android_system_properties, bumpalo, iana-time-zone and iana-time-zone-haiku, js-sys, log,
rustversion, wasm-bindgen and its three wasm-bindgen-* crates, windows-core, windows-implement,
windows-interface, windows-result and windows-strings are locked but not built on Linux. Every
entry's resolved features were refreshed from `cargo metadata` that day (tokio's now include
its multi-thread runtime, processes and io-util). The texts are reproduced from the cached
sources, with futures-channel's embedded notice for Dmitry Vyukov's queue and tracing-core's
src/spin/LICENSE (Mathijs van de Nes; that module is built only without its `std` feature).
sse-stream and base64 0.23.1 joined the graph on 2026-11-05 too, for MCP servers over HTTP
(rmcp's streamable HTTP client), with their texts reproduced from the cached sources, which
carry no embedded notices; every entry's resolved features were refreshed from `cargo metadata`
again (rmcp's, futures-util's and http-body-util's changed).
spellbook joined the graph on 2026-11-06, for spelling in the editor, with its text reproduced
from the cached source, whose src carries no embedded notices (its vendor dictionaries are not
built). The en_US dictionary built into the binary is not a crate: dictionary-en 4.0.0 from npm,
SCOWL's, under the terms its license gives, reproduced after spellbook's entry.
version_check, autocfg, cc, find-msvc-tools, pkg-config and shlex are build dependencies, not
evidence of runtime shipment.
zlib-rs is locked only through flate2's weak `zlib-rs?/std` feature and is not built
(`cargo tree --target all -i zlib-rs` prints nothing); its sources were not audited for
embedded notices.
